== explain data engineering in simple words
  change in ch01-005:
    span          : 'by data scientists, analysts, and other'
    old (0.25): When we unpack the common threads of how various people define data engineering, an obvious pattern emerges: a data engineer gets data, stores it, and prepares it for consumption by data scientists, analysts, and others.
    new (0.5): We define data engineering and data engineer as follows: Data engineering is the development, implementation, and maintenance of systems and processes that take in raw data and produce high-quality, consistent information that supports downstream use cases, such as analysis and machine learning.
  BEFORE (redundancy 0.9423): Data engineers get data, store it, and prepare it for others. [Ch. 1] Data engineering handles moving, changing, and managing data. [Ch. 1] It's easy to focus on new tech and forget the main goal of data engineering. [Ch. 4] Data engineers keep data available for others to use. [Ch. 1]
  AFTER  (redundancy 0.8661): Data engineering makes systems to handle raw data and give clean info for use. [Ch. 1] Data engineering handles moving, changing, and managing data. [Ch. 1] It's easy to focus on new tech and forget the main goal of data engineering. [Ch. 4] Data engineers keep data available for others to use. [Ch. 1]

